# L §3.3 (round 6): "Any pairing with day other than a daily r, or a daily r over a longer period, is refused
# (LOAD-UNIT where load sees the rate's period, RUN-DOMAIN otherwise, §8.4)": r is an input, so load doesn't see its
# period: RUN-DOMAIN at the key.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input r: rate
def p: num = periodic(r, day, simple) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  r = 12 %/year

ask a: p law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: refused: RUN-DOMAIN ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
